First, we find the complementary solution by solving $\mathbf{x}' = A\mathbf{x}$. The characteristic equation is:
\begin{align*}
    \det \begin{pmatrix} 1-\lambda & 4 \\ 1 & 1-\lambda \end{pmatrix} = (1-\lambda)^2 - 4 = \lambda^2 - 2\lambda - 3 = 0
\end{align*}
Factoring yields $(\lambda - 3)(\lambda + 1) = 0$, so the eigenvalues are $\lambda_1 = 3$ and $\lambda_2 = -1$. We find the corresponding eigenvectors. For $\lambda_1 = 3$:
