\begin{align*}
    \begin{pmatrix} 6 & 8 \\ 2 & 6 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\ a_2 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 2 \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
This gives the system $6a_1 + 8a_2 = 6$ and $2a_1 + 6a_2 = 2$. Dividing the second equation by 2 gives $a_1 + 3a_2 = 1$, so $a_1 = 1 - 3a_2$. Substituting into the first equation (divided by 2, which is $3a_1 + 4a_2 = 3$):
\begin{align*}
