\begin{align*}
    \mathbf{b} &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 & 4 \\ 1 & 1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} \\
    &= \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 1 \end{pmatrix} + \begin{pmatrix} -2 \\ -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}
\end{align*}
The particular solution is $\mathbf{x}_p(t) = \begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \cos t + \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} \sin t = \begin{pmatrix} \cos t - \sin t \\ 0 \end{pmatrix}$. Combining the complementary and particular solutions, the general solution is:
\begin{align*}
    x_1(t) &= 2c_1 e^{3t} - 2c_2 e^{-t} + \cos t - \sin t \\
    x_2(t) &= c_1 e^{3t} + c_2 e^{-t}
\end{align*}

